# Which release of simple-metrics (github.com/georgenicoll/simple-metrics) is
# deployed to the Pi, and the SHA-256 of its aarch64 archive.
#
# ./wga downloads that release (tools/fetch_simple_metrics.sh) and refuses it
# unless the archive matches the checksum below. This file is the only thing
# trusted: the checksum is never taken from the download itself, so a release
# that was altered after the fact is caught.
#
# To upgrade: pick the release, then copy the checksum for
# simple-metrics-<version>-aarch64-unknown-linux-musl.tar.gz from the
# SHA256SUMS file on that release's GitHub page, and change both lines.
SIMPLE_METRICS_VERSION=v0.5.3
SIMPLE_METRICS_SHA256=ae4bec8ef3dc4ea1a5886e306a0fdf32733dc1c474271c5845dcbeab928bf912
